                      <div class="fsTitle" id="fsArticle_3551_333">
                        Policy 3250 - STUDENT RECORDS: PROTECTION OF THE RIGHTS
                        AND PRIVACY OF PARENTS AND STUDENTS
                      </div>

                      <div class="fsBody">
                        <p>
                          The Highline School District will maintain student
                          records in a manner that will assure the protection of
                          the rights and privacy of students and
                          parents/guardian. All school district records,&nbsp;
                          data, or information related to individual students
                          shall be treated as confidential. Such information
                          demands judicious use and should always be used so as
                          to contribute to the welfare of the&nbsp; individuals
                          under consideration. Access to student records shall
                          be granted by the custodian of the records only in
                          accordance with the procedures established herein.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                          Legal Reference:&nbsp;<br />
                          Family Education Rights and Privacy Act -&nbsp;CFR 45,
                          Part 99<br />
                          Pupil tests and records-Pupil personnel records-School
                          district policy in writing -&nbsp;WAC 180-52-025<br />
                          General Education Provisions Act (as amended 31
                          December 1974) - Section 438
                        </p>

                        <p>
                          Highline School District 401<br />
                          Adopted by the Board:&nbsp;&nbsp; August 28, 1985
                        </p>
